## Net changes from the `_slots` change feed; a running MV refresh is waited for
================================================================================

Context: the design's P1 "net changes for app-managed Lakebase / Neo4j" read the
`_data` materialized view's change feed, which needs the external-metadata
private preview — `table_changes` on the MV fails `DELTA_LOG_FILE_NOT_FOUND`
on both reachable workspaces (re-checked on the sandbox today after
`REPAIR TABLE … SYNC METADATA`; `DESCRIBE HISTORY` on the MV is refused outright),
so every app-written store fell back to the full stream (`cdf_unavailable`).
When the slot pipeline carries the whole graph (`batch_mappings = 0`) the view
is the `_slots` streaming table deduplicated, and a streaming table's automatic
change feed is GA — verified on the sandbox (`table_changes('…_slots', 1)` lists
the AUTO CDC inserts, `VERSION AS OF` works). The feed now comes from there.

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/ChangeFeedReader.py — `net_changes_sql`,
   `iter_net_changes`, `changeset_ratio` take `distinct_rows` (default `True`,
   the `_data` sum-of-signs reduction). `False` (`_slots`, several slots per
   triple) emits `_snapshot_diff_select`: the triples the feed touched in the
   window whose presence differs between `SELECT DISTINCT … VERSION AS OF
   since` and `… VERSION AS OF until` — a slot deleted while another still
   carries the triple is no change, an update spread over several commits is
   one delete + one insert, a duplicate insert of a present triple is nothing.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinNetChangeApply.py — `feed(pipe)`
   returns `("slots", …_slots)` for strategy `mv` with `batch_mappings == 0`
   and a slots table, else `("data", …_data)`; `apply` reads the version /
   table id / ratio / window from that relation and records it as
   `pipe.feed_relation`; `_base_version` rejects a base recorded on the other
   relation (runs from before the fact default to `data`); the log line names
   the feed. Module docstring explains the choice.
3. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildRunHistory.py — materialization
   fact `feed_relation` (docstring: `data_table_version` is the feed relation's
   version); build/_build_pipeline.py declares `feed_relation` next to
   `data_table_id` (no growth of the frozen `_BuildPipeline`);
   TwinMergeFallback `_complete_skipped` carries the base's `feed_relation`.
4. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py — `refresh(client,
   fqn, *, full, wait_s=600, pause_s=20, sleep)`: `REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW`
   retried while the warehouse answers that a refresh is already running
   (`_REFRESH_IN_PROGRESS`: the live "A refresh is already running in the
   background. You can monitor the previous refresh …", the pipelines API's
   "An active update … already exists", in-progress / being-refreshed /
   concurrent wordings); any other error or the wait running out propagates.
   TwinIncrementalBuild `_apply_views` refreshes through it. Found live: a
   `microbatch` build started 50 s after a source change met the view's
   `TRIGGER ON UPDATE` refresh, failed `incremental_failed:InfrastructureError`
   and fell back to a CTAS — dropping the materialized view, stopping the
   continuous pipeline and losing the net-change base (reproduced twice:
   builds 2 and 6 of the evidence domain; a build 5 s after the change was
   fine, its own refresh ran first with `GROUP_AGGREGATE`).
5. Tests — tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_change_feed_reader.py: the exact
   slot statement, ratio / stream use it, five SQLite reductions (cross-slot
   duplicate, update order, insert-then-delete, several commits of one slot,
   duplicate insert); tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_net_apply.py:
   `TestNetChangeFeed` (slots when the slots carry the whole graph into an MV;
   `_data` for batch mappings / no slot step / no slots table / MERGE),
   `TestSlotFedNetApply` (a row-local-only build reads `table_changes('…_slots',
   6, 9)` + `VERSION AS OF 9` and never the `_data` feed; the relation and its
   version are the recorded base; a base that read `_data` is no base; the
   default fixtures with a batch mapping still read `_data`), the fact in
   `build_run_stats`; tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_materialized_view_builder.py:
   `TestRefresh` (waited for across four wordings, other errors at once, the
   wait running out, FULL forwarded). tests/units/settings/test_deploy_instance_id.py:
   `TestEnsureInstanceTarget` puts a deploy's `resources/_generated_instance_target.yml`
   back after each test — the full suite run concurrently with deploy #12 had
   deleted the target between the two `bundle run` steps, so the MCP app's
   start failed `dev-lakebase-rtm: no such target` (regenerated by hand with
   `ensure_instance_target` + `bundle run mcp_ontobricks_app`; both apps on the
   new deployment).
6. docs/incremental-materialization.md — net-change apply bullet (feed
   relation, snapshot diff, fallback reasons), previews bullet, the microbatch
   refresh paragraph (the wait), Known limitations (the MV-fed apply of a
   `_data` with batch mappings; a registry delete leaves the slot pipeline
   running and every graph object in place — seen live, manual cleanup
   recipe), live verification (the sandbox freshness measurement), the P1
   traceability row (Live ✅ with the figures below).

Sandbox evidence (`ontobricks-rtm`, rebuilt 0.10.0 apps, 2026-11-04), in the
session transcript:
- `tests/external/test_mv_incremental_plan.py::test_the_data_view_plans_an_incremental_refresh`
  PASSED against the sandbox warehouse (the CI `EXPLAIN` check).
- `ZzNetFeedLive` (app-managed Lakebase, `microbatch`, fixture
  `rtm.customers_many` = 60 rows / 120 triples; a 3-row fixture cannot show the
  10 % threshold — one update is 33 %): build 1 full stream, base
  `feed_relation = slots` v5 → (build 2: the refresh race above, CTAS) →
  build 3 full stream, base v8 → one UPDATE → build 4 **`apply_mode =
  net_changes`, `table_changes('…_slots', 9, 12)`, 1 delete + 1 insert, 50 s**
  (full streams of the same graph: 95–180 s); Lakebase `zznetfeedlive_v1_sync`
  120 triples, the new label, zero stale markers; `POST /dtwin/incremental/reconcile`
  → `drift: false`, equal `_slots` / `_data` hashes; build 5 (update 5 s before)
  net_changes v12..v13 with `refresh_technique = GROUP_AGGREGATE`; build 6
  (update 50 s before) reproduced the race.
- Freshness: `scripts/measure_freshness.py` died twice in the Thrift driver on
  this network (`I/O operation on closed file`; `RequestError` on `OpenSession`);
  the same probe over the Statement Execution API: `_slots` 13.2 s / 13.5 s,
  `_data` 319 s (one marker not within 420 s), `_graph` 422 s / 321 s — the MV
  trigger cadence; the fast path reads `_slots` for such a graph.
- Not available on the sandbox: Real-Time compute ("Real-Time compute is not
  enabled for this workspace") and the `_data` MV change feed (above). The
  Lakehouse//RT KPI was therefore measured again on the integration workspace
  (`fevm-ontobricks-int`, its RT warehouse started for the run and stopped
  after; the spike's own tables and continuous slot pipeline, torn down):
  source commit → visible through the fast-path relation on RT **14.95 s
  median, 18.3 s p95 (n = 10)** — the ≤ 30 s p95 KPI — point reads p50 181 ms /
  p95 284 ms; recursive CTE refused by RT as the fallback expects.
- Deploy #12 after the net-change change: the bundle's ACL reconcile dropped
  the app SP's self `CAN_MANAGE` again (every POST answered the Access Denied
  page) — re-granted with `apps update-permissions`; the MCP target episode in
  item 5. Deleting the first evidence domain left its continuous pipeline
  RUNNING and all UC / Lakebase objects (item 6) — stopped / dropped by hand.
- Deploy #13 with the refresh wait (both apps RUNNING on it; `/health` 0.10.0;
  the SP re-grant again). Build 7 re-created the MV after build 6's CTAS (full
  stream, base `feed_relation = slots` v14). Build 8, started 50 s after a
  source UPDATE exactly as builds 2 and 6: `MaterializedViewBuilder.refresh`
  logged "A refresh of …_data is already running; waiting 20s (attempt 1/30 …
  9/30)" against the view's trigger refresh, the tenth attempt went through,
  the build stayed `microbatch` (`strategy = mv`, no fallback reason) and
  applied the net changes of `_slots` v14..v16 — 1 delete + 1 insert — in 329 s
  instead of demoting the domain to a CTAS. The evidence domain, its pipeline,
  UC relations, Lakebase objects and the fixture table were removed afterwards
  (`/tmp` scripts, not committed).

